{"id": "tea:pancadasi:1.15-17", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "1.15-17"}, "paraphrase": "Prakṛti, with the reflection of Brahman in it, is twofold: with pure sattva it is māyā, and Brahman reflected in it, controlling it, is the omniscient Īśvara; with impure sattva it is avidyā, and the reflection subject to it is the jīva, many owing to its variety; this avidyā is the causal body, and the jīva identifying with it is prājña.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:maya", "trm:avidya", "trm:isvara", "trm:jiva", "trm:karana-sarira", "trm:prajna"], "concepts": ["cpt:isvara-advaita", "cpt:jiva-advaita", "cpt:pratibimba-vada"], "disputes": ["dsp:maya-avidya-distinction", "dsp:how-the-one-appears-as-many"], "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:1.3", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "1.3"}, "original": {"text": "śabdasparśādayo vedyā vaicitryāj jāgare pṛthak / tato vibhaktā tatsaṃvid aikarūpyān na bhidyate", "script": "IAST", "edition": "vulgate wording recalled from memory (verify against an edition)", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "paraphrase": "Sound, touch and the other objects known in waking differ from one another; distinct from them, the consciousness of them, being uniform, does not differ.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:saksin", "cpt:three-states-and-turiya"], "practices": ["prc:drg-drsya-viveka", "prc:avastha-traya-viveka"], "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:10", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "The witness is like the lamp in a theatre: it illumines the patron (the ego), the audience (the objects), the dancer (the intellect) and the musicians (the senses) alike, and goes on shining when they have left.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:saksin"], "concepts": ["cpt:saksin"], "practices": ["prc:saksi-bhava"], "notes": "Chapter 10 (Nāṭakadīpa).", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:15", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "15"}, "paraphrase": "The joy of objects is a fragment of the bliss of Brahman, appearing when a desire is satisfied and the mind becomes briefly inward and calm; all beings live on a portion of that bliss.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:bliss-advaita"], "cross_refs": ["tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad:4.3.32"], "notes": "Chapter 15 (Viṣayānanda).", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:6", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "As a canvas is washed, starched, outlined and coloured, so the supreme self is pure consciousness, the inner controller (antaryāmin), the cosmic subtle being (Hiraṇyagarbha) and the cosmic gross being (Virāj); the painted figures are the beings, and the painted clothes on them the semblance of consciousness (cidābhāsa).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:antaryamin", "trm:hiranyagarbha", "trm:virat", "trm:cidabhasa"], "concepts": ["cpt:samasti-vyasti", "cpt:creation-advaita"], "notes": "Chapter 6 (Citradīpa), opening verses.", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:6/2", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "Four 'spaces' illustrate the four aspects of consciousness: pot-space (the immutable witness in the body, kūṭastha), great space (Brahman), space reflected in the water of the pot (the jīva) and space reflected in the moisture of clouds (Īśvara).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:kutastha", "trm:ghatakasa"], "concepts": ["cpt:pot-space", "cpt:reflection-analogy"], "disputes": ["dsp:how-the-one-appears-as-many"], "notes": "Chapter 6 (Citradīpa).", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:7", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "Chapter 7 expounds BĀU 4.4.12 ('if a person knows the self as I am this, desiring what, for whose sake, should he suffer along with the body?'), and lists seven states of the jīva: ignorance, veiling, projection, mediate knowledge, immediate knowledge, cessation of sorrow, and unrestricted contentment.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:seven-states-of-jiva"], "paths": ["pth:pancadasi-seven-states"], "cross_refs": ["tea:brhadaranyaka-upanisad:4.4.12"], "notes": "Chapter 7 (Tṛptidīpa); verse locator of the list (c. 7.33) low confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:7/2", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "The tenth man: ten men who crossed a river count themselves, each forgetting to count himself, and grieve for the 'lost' tenth; told 'there is a tenth', they know it mediately; told 'you are the tenth', each knows it immediately and grief ends — so the mahāvākya gives immediate knowledge of the self.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:dasama", "trm:aparoksa-jnana", "trm:paroksa-jnana"], "concepts": ["cpt:tenth-man", "cpt:seven-states-of-jiva"], "disputes": ["dsp:sravana-alone-liberates"], "notes": "Chapter 7.", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:8", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "8"}, "paraphrase": "The immutable (kūṭastha) consciousness, the substratum of both bodies, is distinct from the semblance of consciousness (cidābhāsa) that animates the intellect; the jīva is the two taken together, and discrimination separates them.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:kutastha", "trm:cidabhasa"], "concepts": ["cpt:saksin", "cpt:abhasa-vada"], "notes": "Chapter 8 (Kūṭasthadīpa).", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:9", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "Meditation on the attributeless Brahman, though an act of mind, leads to liberating knowledge, as mistaking the light of a gem for the gem leads one to the gem (a 'consistent error', saṃvādi-bhrama); inquiry is best, but those unable to inquire should meditate.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:samvadi-bhrama", "trm:upasana"], "practices": ["prc:nirguna-upasana"], "concepts": ["cpt:upasana-advaita"], "notes": "Chapter 9 (Dhyānadīpa).", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pancadasi:9/2", "source": "src:pancadasi", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "Obstructions to knowledge are present (attachment to objects, dullness of intellect, perverse reasoning, obstinate misconception), past (earlier tendencies) and future (karma requiring further births); hearing and the rest remove the present ones.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "obstacles": ["obs:pratibandha"], "notes": "Chapter 9; placement low confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
